# BUG-260819-34ikhl independent review

## Verdict
Changes requested.

## Finding
The actor check-and-register transition is atomic and missed-wakeup safe on the success path. However, ResourceRecorder.waitUntilStarted registers a CheckedContinuation that only record(directory:socket:) can resume. If ResourceCommand throws before record during temporary-directory creation, marker write, Unix socket creation/bind, or managed-task registration, HarnessApplication.run completes with commandFailed while cancellationCleanup remains suspended before joining run.value. Test-task cancellation also cannot release the non-throwing waiter. This is an indefinite hang and waiter leak on the explicit startup-failure/cancellation path required by the reviewer contract.

Required rework: preserve explicit actor event synchronization and exact cleanup assertions, but model readiness as a terminal state that publishes either ready or command completion/failure, releases all waiters exactly once on readiness, failure, and cancellation, and add a deterministic regression test for pre-readiness startup failure.

## Independent gates
- Focused stress under four CPU-load workers: swift test --filter HarnessTests/cancellationCleanup; exit 0; 50 parameterized cases passed in 0.018s.
- Clean full suite: swift package clean && swift test; exit 0; 443 tests in 37 suites passed with 25 declared known issues.
- Coverage: swift test --enable-code-coverage; exit 0; 443 tests in 37 suites passed with the same 25 declared known issues.
- Strict formatting: swift format lint --strict --recursive Sources Tests Package.swift; exit 0.
- Boundaries: ./scripts/check-core-boundaries.sh; exit 0.
- Whitespace: git diff --check; exit 0.
- Board validation: task-board validate; exit 0.

## Safety
Review was build-only and privacy-safe. No signing, installation, application/provider launch, VPN preference mutation, VPN activation, route change, or DNS change ran.
